  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Trained teachers for improved learning outcomes in Eastern Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The achievement of SDG 4 relies heavily on teachers, yet progress is constrained by three major challenges: (i) teacher shortages; (ii) qualifications and emerging professional development needs; and (ii) the status and working conditions of teachers and education personnel. The COVID-19 pandemic has further accelerated the need to transform teaching and to better support teachers to respond to a variety of situations and learning needs. UNESCO will continue to explore how governments, teacher education institutions and other stakeholders can better prepare and support teachers to address the challenges and steer progress in order to revert learning loss and enhance capacities for inclusive teaching and learning. UNESCO will support Member States in (i) the delivery of teacher education and (ii) the review, development and implementation of teacher policies.</narrative>
  </description>
